(2421390, 334102, 43405, '<td valign="top">LOL.... Timing is spot on :)</td>', 'LOL.... Timing is spot on :)', '2006-05-16 17:16:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421402, 333373, 54731, '<td valign="top">I think there''s excessive dodging on her face, otherwise it''s great! love the lighting.</td>', 'I think there''s excessive dodging on her face, otherwise it''s great! love the lighting.', '2006-05-16 17:22:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421417, 333975, 3087, '<td valign="top">What a sweet portrait though expression feels either a touch forced or perhaps mid-change? I like the pose a lot, leaning on the ledge with elbows out. The environment doesn''t really seem to tell me much about him - I doubt he''s one of those who has written the graffiti - too young - and I can''t work out whether this is a park he plays in or something else?</td>', 'What a sweet portrait though expression feels either a touch forced or perhaps mid-change? I like the pose a lot, leaning on the ledge with elbows out. The environment doesn''t really seem to tell me much about him - I doubt he''s one of those who has written the graffiti - too young - and I can''t work out whether this is a park he plays in or something else?', '2006-05-16 17:31:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421433, 332737, 43405, '<td valign="top">Certainly a nice GSP. Good photograpg, eyes clear and I like the expression on the face. Two things though, I think the photograph would have been just that much better if you had got the front paws too. 7<br/>The second (didn''t affect my vote) but I think the subject would have looked better without the shock collar.... but then again I suppose it adds some weight to the hunting theme. Well done</td>', 'Certainly a nice GSP. Good photograpg, eyes clear and I like the expression on the face. Two things though, I think the photograph would have been just that much better if you had got the front paws too. 7The second (didn''t affect my vote) but I think the subject would have looked better without the shock collar.... but then again I suppose it adds some weight to the hunting theme. Well done', '2006-05-16 17:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421450, 334553, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''d be interested to know in what way you see this as more than just a dog in a landscape - because, for me, it lacks any real sense of personality in the dog, any sense of his character, which i think is required by this challenge, no? The shot is pretty well executed - although the highlights go very quickly in the clouds.</td>', 'I''d be interested to know in what way you see this as more than just a dog in a landscape - because, for me, it lacks any real sense of personality in the dog, any sense of his character, which i think is required by this challenge, no? The shot is pretty well executed - although the highlights go very quickly in the clouds.', '2006-05-16 17:40:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421456, 333878, 6999, '<td valign="top">I like. Tonality is very well done. One might quibble with the balance of environment and portrait - how much of this machine do you actually need in the shot to give that impact? - and getting closer to him would give us more information, more character. There is a strong sense of the machine though, of the mechanical.</td>', 'I like. Tonality is very well done. One might quibble with the balance of environment and portrait - how much of this machine do you actually need in the shot to give that impact? - and getting closer to him would give us more information, more character. There is a strong sense of the machine though, of the mechanical.', '2006-05-16 17:42:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421469, 334236, 6999, '<td valign="top">Well done - technically, almost boringly ''perfect'' - and kind of camply, well, obvious? For me it''s just a portrait with a couple of props thrown in to get that required element, rather than telling me anything interesting about this bloke. Right down to colouring the lamps, and the carefully revealed logo on the tripod, it smacks of an attempt to fulfill an idea of what the community likes. Kind of a shame, given such technical finesse.</td>', 'Well done - technically, almost boringly ''perfect'' - and kind of camply, well, obvious? For me it''s just a portrait with a couple of props thrown in to get that required element, rather than telling me anything interesting about this bloke. Right down to colouring the lamps, and the carefully revealed logo on the tripod, it smacks of an attempt to fulfill an idea of what the community likes. Kind of a shame, given such technical finesse.', '2006-05-16 17:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421485, 334295, 6999, '<td valign="top">Perhaps, making it plain enough that she is injecting herself without having to put that in the title would make a more effective photograph. You selective de-sat actually works against what your title suggests is the intent of this image, dragging the attention to completely the wrong place on the figure. It has potential though, this shot - but I don''t think it succeeds; and that de-sat remains mystifying.</td>', 'Perhaps, making it plain enough that she is injecting herself without having to put that in the title would make a more effective photograph. You selective de-sat actually works against what your title suggests is the intent of this image, dragging the attention to completely the wrong place on the figure. It has potential though, this shot - but I don''t think it succeeds; and that de-sat remains mystifying.', '2006-05-16 17:49:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2421486, 334199, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good work - tells me something about this man, for the inclusion of his world.</td>', 'Good work - tells me something about this man, for the inclusion of his world.', '2006-05-16 17:50:29.000000', NULL, 1),
